<main id="main">

<section class="th-hero"><div class="th-w th-hero-g"><div class="th-hero-t"><p class="th-code">theorem 1.0 &mdash; maths, made clear</p><h1>Understand <span class="th-hl">why</span>, not just how.</h1><p class="th-lead">Theorem is a calm, independent maths site. We explain big ideas step by step, then hand you tools to test them yourself: drag a triangle, graph a parabola, and see the proof in action.</p>
<div class="th-hero-a"><a class="th-btn" href="#pyth">Explore Pythagoras</a><a class="th-btn th-btn-o" href="#quad">Graph a quadratic</a></div><dl class="th-ax"><div><dt>Lemma</dt><dd>Small steps</dd></div><div><dt>Theorem</dt><dd>Big ideas</dd></div><div><dt>Proof</dt><dd>Why it&rsquo;s true</dd></div></dl></div>
<div class="th-board"><div class="th-board-in"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1758685734640-5a539c096aed?auto=format&fit=crop&w=640&h=440&q=75" alt="a professor writing equations on a blackboard" width="640" height="440" fetchpriority="high"></figure><div class="th-chalk" aria-hidden="true"><span style="--i:0">a&sup2; + b&sup2; = c&sup2;</span><span style="--i:1">x = (&minus;b &plusmn; &radic;(b&sup2; &minus; 4ac)) / 2a</span><span style="--i:2">&pi; &asymp; 3.14159</span><span style="--i:3">&sum; 1/n&sup2; = &pi;&sup2;/6</span><span style="--i:4">e<sup>i&pi;</sup> + 1 = 0</span><span style="--i:5">A = &pi;r&sup2;</span><span style="--i:6">sin&sup2;&theta; + cos&sup2;&theta; = 1</span><span style="--i:7">&there4; QED</span></div></div><div class="th-tray" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div></div></div></section>

<section class="th-s th-py" id="pyth"><div class="th-w"><div class="th-sh"><p class="th-code">// tool one</p><h2 class="rv">Right-triangle explorer</h2><p class="th-p">Change the two shorter sides. The squares on each side redraw, and you can watch a&sup2; + b&sup2; always add up to c&sup2;.</p></div>
<div class="th-py-g"><div class="th-paper"><svg viewBox="0 0 420 420" id="py-s" role="img" aria-label="Right triangle with squares on each side"><g id="py-g"></g></svg></div>
<div><div class="th-ctl"><label class="th-lb" for="py-a">side a = <b id="py-av">3</b></label><input type="range" id="py-a" min="1" max="8" step="1" value="3" class="th-rng"><label class="th-lb" for="py-b">side b = <b id="py-bv">4</b></label><input type="range" id="py-b" min="1" max="8" step="1" value="4" class="th-rng"></div>
<div class="th-eq" aria-live="polite"><p class="th-eq-l"><span class="ca" id="py-a2">9</span> + <span class="cb" id="py-b2">16</span> = <span class="cc" id="py-c2">25</span></p><p class="th-eq-c">c = &radic;<span id="py-c2b">25</span> = <b id="py-c">5</b></p><p class="th-eq-n" id="py-n">A Pythagorean triple: all three sides are whole numbers.</p></div><figure class="th-py-i rv rv-c"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1777639629833-49b027b5480e?auto=format&fit=crop&w=520&h=260&q=75" alt="a wooden protractor resting on a chalkboard" width="520" height="260" loading="lazy"></figure></div></div></div></section>

<section class="th-s th-qd" id="quad"><div class="th-w th-qd-g"><div><p class="th-code">// tool two</p><h2 class="rv">Quadratic grapher</h2><p class="th-p">Set the coefficients of y = ax&sup2; + bx + c. The parabola, its roots and its vertex update instantly.</p>
<div class="th-coef"><label>a<input type="number" id="qd-a" value="1" step="0.5" min="-5" max="5"></label><label>b<input type="number" id="qd-b" value="-2" step="1" min="-10" max="10"></label><label>c<input type="number" id="qd-c" value="-3" step="1" min="-10" max="10"></label></div>
<p class="th-fn" id="qd-f" aria-live="polite">y = x&sup2; &minus; 2x &minus; 3</p><dl class="th-qr" aria-live="polite"><div><dt>Discriminant</dt><dd id="qd-d">16</dd></div><div><dt>Roots</dt><dd id="qd-r">x = &minus;1, 3</dd></div><div><dt>Vertex</dt><dd id="qd-v">(1, &minus;4)</dd></div></dl><p class="th-small" id="qd-n"></p><figure class="th-qd-i rv rv-c"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1787639543507-16b87d0e1b8a?auto=format&fit=crop&w=520&h=200&q=75" alt="blue grid lines on square panels" width="520" height="200" loading="lazy"></figure></div>
<div class="th-graph"><svg viewBox="0 0 400 400" id="qd-s" role="img" aria-label="Graph of the parabola"><defs><pattern id="thg" width="20" height="20" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse"><path d="M20 0H0V20" fill="none" stroke="#CFE0F2" stroke-width="1"/></pattern></defs><rect width="400" height="400" fill="url(#thg)"/><path d="M0 200H400M200 0V400" stroke="#2B3A8F" stroke-width="1.5"/><path id="qd-p" d="" fill="none" stroke="#E8604C" stroke-width="3.5" stroke-linecap="round"/><g id="qd-pts"></g></svg><p class="th-graph-k">each square = 1 unit</p></div></div></section>

<section class="th-s th-kit"><div class="th-w"><div class="th-sh th-sh-c"><p class="th-code">// the toolkit</p><h2 class="rv">Instruments of reason</h2></div><ul class="th-kit-l stg"><li class="rv"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1503789101408-444b37749472?auto=format&fit=crop&w=320&h=240&q=75" alt="two drawing compasses on a surface" width="320" height="240" loading="lazy"></figure><code>tool.01</code><b>Compass</b><p>Draws circles and copies lengths exactly.</p></li><li class="rv"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1645830887841-2542fa41378e?auto=format&fit=crop&w=320&h=240&q=75" alt="a wooden ruler and set square on a blue background" width="320" height="240" loading="lazy"></figure><code>tool.02</code><b>Ruler &amp; set square</b><p>Straight lines, parallels and right angles.</p></li><li class="rv"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1768839720849-fef976b3ffff?auto=format&fit=crop&w=320&h=240&q=75" alt="a teal calculator and a white pen" width="320" height="240" loading="lazy"></figure><code>tool.03</code><b>Calculator</b><p>Checks arithmetic so you can focus on ideas.</p></li><li class="rv"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1777639629986-b2d1138e8fe2?auto=format&fit=crop&w=320&h=240&q=75" alt="an old wooden abacus on a blue surface" width="320" height="240" loading="lazy"></figure><code>tool.04</code><b>Abacus</b><p>Place value you can touch and move.</p></li></ul></div></section>

<section class="th-tl"><div class="th-w th-tl-g"><figure class="th-tl-i rv"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1760238470874-721a75f86bec?auto=format&fit=crop&w=520&h=520&q=75" alt="a colourful geometric cube pattern" width="520" height="520" loading="lazy"></figure><div><p class="th-code">// a very short history</p><h2 class="rv">Four thousand years of proof</h2><ol class="th-tl-l"><li class="rv"><code>c. 1800 BC</code><p>A Babylonian clay tablet lists Pythagorean triples.</p></li><li class="rv"><code>c. 300 BC</code><p>Euclid&rsquo;s Elements builds geometry from five axioms.</p></li><li class="rv"><code>1637</code><p>Descartes joins algebra and geometry with coordinates.</p></li><li class="rv"><code>1995</code><p>Wiles completes a proof of Fermat&rsquo;s Last Theorem.</p></li></ol></div></div></section>

<section class="th-gd"><div class="th-w th-gd-g"><a class="th-gc rv" href="pythagorean-theorem-guide.html"><code>Theorem 1</code><b>The Pythagorean Theorem</b><p>What it says, why it&rsquo;s true and where you&rsquo;ll use it.</p><span class="th-gc-f" aria-hidden="true">a&sup2;+b&sup2;=c&sup2;</span></a><a class="th-gc th-gc-b rv" href="how-to-read-a-proof-guide.html"><code>Theorem 2</code><b>How to Read a Proof</b><p>Axioms, logic and the steps that lead to &there4;.</p><span class="th-gc-f" aria-hidden="true">P &rArr; Q</span></a></div></section>

</main>
